  "reading": [
   "Pallas: grid always 256 lanes (2*B*T_MAX); valid lanes 48% in phase 1 and 24% in phase 2 (phase 2 pads to 2B by design + T_MAX padding); launched/useful lane-sweeps 3.5x (ph1) and 4.7x (ph2), but dead lanes exit at once: per useful lane-sweep 0.125 ns/grid point, identical in both phases",
   "lane imbalance: mean sweeps per valid lane 53 (ph1) / 79 (ph2) vs mean per-call max 89 / 91 -> the last ~40% of half-sweep launches run a shrinking set of lanes; ~2 x 90 = 180 half-sweep launches per phase per site batch (~2,000 launches per state)",
   "XLA pool: executed/useful lane-sweeps 2.6x (ph1), 3.1x (ph2) (lockstep width 256/64/16); 0.46 ns per executed lane-sweep point = 3.7x the Pallas cost per useful lane-sweep; x waste -> 9.5-11.8x SOR",
   "CPU: 8.3 ns per executed lane-sweep point (18x the XLA-A40 per-sweep cost), same 2.6-2.9x lockstep waste",
   "roofline (estimate): ~10-12 B/point/half-sweep from DRAM at 696 GB/s ~ 0.03-0.035 ns per lane-sweep point; Pallas achieves 0.125 -> ~3.5-4x off the bandwidth roof (each half-sweep reads/writes every point of the block but updates half; 7 phi + 4 code loads per point uncached)"
  ]
 },
